WEBVTT

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:16.880
would result in a great amount of damage.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.890
Many of our cities' military targets would be heavily damaged.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.380
However, even in an extensive attack,

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.740
the total area affected by the blast and thermal effects

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.960
would be fairly small in relation to the total area of the country.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.700
This would not be the case with radioactive fallout.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.600
The area affected by fallout would be many times larger than the area affected by the explosion.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:44.470
Radioactive fallout from enemy weapons could threaten life anywhere in the country.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.590
Radioactive fallout, then, could be a serious threat to almost everyone in the United States.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.750
Fortunately, protection against this threat can be achieved at comparatively little cost per person

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.590
by intelligent community planning.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.960
aid communities in Plans

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.480
and organizing protection against fallout, the Office of Civil Defense has set up a nationwide shelter program.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:13.550
The object of this program is to survey, mark, and provision existing public shelter spaces

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:20.340
and develop enough additional shelters to protect the entire population against radioactive fallout in case of attack.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:25.370
Before attempting to select or identify shelters, however,

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.670
we must first understand what constitutes adequate protection against fallout.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:35.570
Fallout from a nuclear cloud can be expected to settle on rooftops, lawns, fields, streets,

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:41.960
trees, sidewalks, on any surface in fact where dust might collect. Of course radioactive materials

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:46.440
generally cannot be seen with the naked eye. Fallout is illustrated in this graphic to show

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:51.680
it descending. From this fallout will come different kinds of radiation, the most dangerous

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:58.150
of which is gamma rays. Gamma rays like x-rays are quite penetrating. They're also quite destructive

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.190
to human tissue

00:06:59.190 --> 00:06:59.850
and may produce

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.810
severe illness or death to anyone not properly shielded from them, and the danger increases

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:09.530
in direct proportion to the length and amount of exposure, or in other words, the dosage.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:15.550
Since fallout may remain dangerous for a period of days or even weeks, a shelter must be able

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:19.490
to provide enough protection so that its occupants will not accumulate a dangerous

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.610
dose of radiation during their stay in the shelter.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:28.940
This ability to shield its occupants from radiation is known as a shelter's protection factor.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:43.190
A shelter having a protection factor of 100, for instance, means simply that a person inside the shelter will receive only one one-hundredth as much radiation as a person outside with no protection at all.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:53.360
If this man outside receives a dose of 800 rentkins in a given period of time, the man inside will receive only eight rentkins during the same period.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:59.980
In other words, the man outside would probably receive a fatal dose of radiation if received in a short time.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.960
while the man inside the shelter would be unharmed. Why? Because of the type and

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:11.270
amount of material which lies between this man and the source of radiation.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.860
Generally speaking, any substance will offer some form of protection against

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:20.860
radiation. The heavier the substance, the greater the mass, the better the

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:26.230
protection. Shielding quality of any material is directly related to its

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.850
weight per cubic foot. That's why heavy, dense material...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.860
Materials such as concrete or masonry provide much better protection than lightweight materials

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:37.020
of the same thickness, such as wood or plaster.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:42.620
Even steel or glass have high shielding ability, but they're ordinarily used in such thin

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.100
sheets that they provide very little actual protection.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:49.920
Their sand also provide good protection if the protective layer is thick enough.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:56.310
In short, the best shelter will be found where there is a large mass of heavy material between

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.390
the occupants and the source of radiation.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.620
principal types of fallout shelters, the family or home shelter and public shelter.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:10.970
In many rural areas, the family type shelter is the only practical one, since it's the

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:14.450
only one which would be easily accessible to the people who need protection.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:19.310
Also in many rural areas, public shelter facilities are very limited.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:25.240
In some cases, existing structures are readily available, such as the tornado shelters,

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:28.620
so often found on the farms of Kansas, Nebraska, and Oklahoma.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.640
protection against radiation must be provided for the doorway.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.740
In other cases, suitable shelters would have to be built,

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:41.420
either in basements, if available, or in convenient locations nearby.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:46.050
However, public shelters have several advantages over family shelters.

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:50.730
For this reason, the National Shelter Program is placing emphasis on

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.450
identifying, modifying public shelters.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.940
To locate and mark all suitable public shelter space, a nationwide service

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.440
survey has been conducted by specially trained architects and engineers.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:09.240
In towns and cities all over the country, these men have examined all types and kinds of buildings

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:13.260
to determine exactly what space is available in existing structures.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:19.150
To be acceptable under the National Shelter Program, shelter space must meet the minimum

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.590
protection factor required by the federal government.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:25.710
Such space is most likely to be found in the basements of banks.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:37.930
public building, in the inner core of large substantial buildings such as hospitals, apartment

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:44.410
houses, older type school buildings, or large office buildings.

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:48.820
In many of these buildings, a surprising amount of space may prove to be suitable.

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:54.800
In this building, for instance, not only the basement would provide excellent shelter,

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:57.110
but also many of the upper floors.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:10:59.460
The two top floors, however,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.940
could be hazardous because of their proximity

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:04.000
to the fallout which would settle on the roof.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:07.260
And the ground floor might not be usable

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.420
because of the fallout collecting on the ground.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:12.950
Still, this building would have more than enough space

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.910
to shelter all of the people normally living or working here.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:20.220
Suitable space can also be found in the outlying areas

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:22.680
of cities, such as shopping centers,

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.650
especially where there are basement selling or storage

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:29.960
areas, in certain types of factory building, in

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.190
firehouses, and buildings are not the only places to look. Suitable shelters can also be found in

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:42.930
mines, especially drift mines, where the shaft is driven into the side of a hill, or in caves,

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:52.250
or in highway or railroad tunnels, or in subways. However, in some rural areas,

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:58.770
shelters can also be found in wine cellars, such as those found in California or western New York

00:11:58.770 --> 00:11:59.070
State.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:06.150
in large potato cellars, such as those in southern Idaho. Of course, adequate protection against

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:12.860
fallout must be provided for the entryway. We must remember that shelters are not strange or unique

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:18.750
structures with mysterious protective qualities. Rather, they are regular, everyday structures

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:25.880
which are all around us. What we must be able to do is recognize their ability to protect us. Size

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:29.980
must also be considered. Is the space large enough to...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.160
house the minimum number of people required by the government? Or is it too

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:40.260
small to be approved as a public shelter? Then there is the matter of location. Is

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:45.720
the space located in an area where shelter space is needed? Or is it too far from

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:51.070
the people who will be expected to use it? And there are health factors. While the

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:56.250
object of the shelter program must be survival rather than comfort, there are

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:59.970
certain essential minimum health standards. Does the space

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.440
have the ability to maintain bearable temperature and humidity conditions when

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:09.320
filled to capacity? Is the air supply sufficient for the number of occupants?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:16.720
Even when inactive, people require fresh air. These factors, protection, size,

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:22.570
location, must be considered when selecting space for shelter under the

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:27.470
government survey. If suitable, the space is eligible for marking with the

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.900
approved Civil Defense Shelter sign.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.280
and for provisioning with the supplies furnished by the federal government.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:42.260
These include water and food supplies, medical kits, sanitation kits, and shelter radiation kits.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:49.320
The shelter space which will be identified through this nationwide survey

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.590
will not be enough to accommodate all of the American people.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:56.360
Other space will have to be improved or constructed.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.960
One way that space can be made usable is by...

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:05.800
fairly simple modifications of existing buildings. Certain types of buildings, of course, lend

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:11.140
themselves to modification more readily than others. A solidly constructed building, such

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:16.130
as this, for instance, may have a good large basement, which needs only to have certain

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:21.640
unnecessary windows bricked up to make it an excellent shelter space. Or this well-built

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:27.570
hospital may very well have a basement which would provide ample shelter space. A baffle

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.970
wall were constructed in front of an outside door.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.830
or opening to serve as a shield or barrier against radiation.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.570
The space within could serve as a shelter.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.810
Also, additional shelter space can often be provided by

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:43.190
expanding the capacity of existing shelters.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:47.650
In some cases, it may be possible to double the capacity of a shelter

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:51.510
simply by installing a fan to provide a greater flow of air.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:57.230
In other cases, it may be possible to brick up unnecessary doors leading into room

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.960
and thereby increase the amount of protection.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.140
and usable space in the hall. Some buildings on the other hand do not lend

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:09.300
themselves to modification which will produce suitable shelter space. These

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:13.440
include modern one-story school buildings which have large glass areas

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:20.910
and no basements, modern one-story factory building, and the average motel. In

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:24.230
all such buildings it would be difficult and costly to provide adequate

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:29.520
protection against fallout collecting on the roof and ground. In any case we must

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:29.860
remember

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.430
that protection is a relative thing, and even substandard space, which does not fully

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:40.190
meet the government requirements regarding size, ventilation, or protection factor, may

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:43.350
still be useful in an emergency and should not be forgotten.

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:50.080
Whatever the difficulties, the goal of each community should be the same, to provide adequate

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:53.600
protection against fallout for every man, woman, and child.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:59.700
Until this goal is met, no community can be said to have an adequate shelter program.

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:00.910
Remember.

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:06.250
Fallout is a real and serious threat as long as there is a threat of a nuclear war.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:07.810
but fallout.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.340
is one threat which we can do something about.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:14.480
by cooperating wholeheartedly with the National Shelter Program.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:19.320
by helping to improve or increase the shelter space in our towns and cities.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.950
we can help to ensure not only our own survival.

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.060
but the survival of our families.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:26.250
our communities.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:27.720
and our nation.

